  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000001_create_users_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000001_create_users_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the initial `users` table and an index for the QuikChat backend database.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `users`: Table to store user information.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `username` (VARCHAR(50), UNIQUE, NOT NULL), `password_hash` (VARCHAR(255), NOT NULL), `display_name` (VARCHAR(50), NOT NULL), `profile_image_url` (VARCHAR(255)), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()), `updated_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()), `last_seen_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ).\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_users_username`: An index on the `username` column of the `users` table for efficient lookups.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000002_create_friend_requests_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000002_create_friend_requests_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `friend_requests` table, define a custom `friend_request_status` ENUM type, and add indexes for efficient querying.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Types**:\n    - `friend_request_status`: An ENUM type with values 'pending', 'accepted', 'declined'.\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `friend_requests`: Table to store friend request information.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `sender_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `receiver_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `status` (friend_request_status, NOT NULL, DEFAULT 'pending'), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()), `updated_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n  - **Database Constraints**:\n    - `UNIQUE(sender_id, receiver_id)`: Ensures that there can only be one pending/active request between any two users.\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_friend_requests_sender_id`: Index on `sender_id` for faster lookups of sent requests.\n    - `idx_friend_requests_receiver_id`: Index on `receiver_id` for faster lookups of received requests.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000003_create_user_blocks_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000003_create_user_blocks_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `user_blocks` table and an index for managing user blocking relationships.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `user_blocks`: Table to store which user has blocked another user.\n      - Fields: `blocker_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `blocked_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n  - **Database Constraints**:\n    - `PRIMARY KEY (blocker_id, blocked_id)`: Ensures that a user can only block another specific user once.\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_user_blocks_blocked_id`: Index on `blocked_id` for efficient lookups of who a user has blocked.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000004_create_conversations_and_participants_tables.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000004_create_conversations_and_participants_tables.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `conversations` and `conversation_participants` tables, define a custom `conversation_type` ENUM, and add an index.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Types**:\n    - `conversation_type`: An ENUM type with values 'private', 'group'.\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `conversations`: Table to store chat conversation metadata.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `type` (conversation_type, NOT NULL), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n    - `conversation_participants`: Junction table to link users to conversations.\n      - Fields: `conversation_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `conversations`), `user_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `joined_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n  - **Database Constraints**:\n    - `PRIMARY KEY (conversation_id, user_id)`: Ensures uniqueness for each participant in a conversation.\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_conversation_participants_user_id`: Index on `user_id` for efficient lookups of conversations a user is part of.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000005_create_messages_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000005_create_messages_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `messages` table, define a custom `message_type` ENUM, and add indexes for efficient querying.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Types**:\n    - `message_type`: An ENUM type with values 'text', 'media'.\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `messages`: Table to store chat message information.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `conversation_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `conversations`), `sender_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users`), `type` (message_type, NOT NULL, DEFAULT 'text'), `content` (TEXT, NOT NULL), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_messages_conversation_id_created_at`: Index on `conversation_id` and `created_at` (descending) for efficient retrieval of messages in a conversation.\n    - `idx_messages_conversation_id_id`: Index on `conversation_id` and `id` (descending) for cursor-based pagination.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000006_create_groups_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000006_create_groups_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `groups` and `group_members` tables, define a custom `group_role` ENUM type, and add indexes for efficient querying and searching.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Types**:\n    - `group_role`: An ENUM type with values 'owner', 'admin', 'member', representing a user's role within a group.\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `groups`: Table to store metadata for chat groups.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `name` (VARCHAR), `tag` (VARCHAR, UNIQUE, NOT NULL), `description` (TEXT), `profile_image_url` (VARCHAR), `created_by` (BIGINT, FK to `users`), `conversation_id` (BIGINT, FK to `conversations`, ON DELETE CASCADE), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ), `updated_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ).\n    - `group_members`: Junction table to link users to groups and define their roles.\n      - Fields: `group_id` (BIGINT, FK to `groups`, ON DELETE CASCADE), `user_id` (BIGINT, FK to `users`, ON DELETE CASCADE), `role` (group_role, DEFAULT 'member'), `joined_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ).\n  - **Database Constraints**:\n    - `PRIMARY KEY (group_id, user_id)` on `group_members`.\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_groups_tag`: Index on the `tag` column of the `groups` table.\n    - `idx_groups_tag_trgm`: GIN index on the `tag` column of the `groups` table, enabling trigram-based similarity searches.\n    - `idx_group_members_user_id`: Index on the `user_id` column of the `group_members` table for efficient lookups of groups a user belongs to.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Database Migration: Defines schema changes for new features.\n  - ENUM Type: Uses a custom ENUM for structured role management.\n  - Foreign Keys: Establishes relationships between `groups`, `users`, and `conversations`.\n  - `pg_trgm` Extension: Utilizes PostgreSQL's trigram extension for fuzzy text searching on group tags.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/migrations/000007_create_notifications_table.up.sql": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/migrations/000007_create_notifications_table.up.sql`\n- High-Level Purpose: SQL script to create the `notifications` table, define a custom `notification_type` ENUM, and add an index for efficient querying.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Database Types**:\n    - `notification_type`: An ENUM type with values 'friend_request_received', 'friend_request_accepted', 'group_invite', 'new_message'.\n  - **Database Tables**:\n    - `notifications`: Table to store user notifications.\n      - Fields: `id` (BIGSERIAL, PRIMARY KEY), `user_id` (BIGINT, NOT NULL, REFERENCES `users` ON DELETE CASCADE), `type` (notification_type, NOT NULL), `message` (TEXT, NOT NULL), `read` (BOOLEAN, NOT NULL, DEFAULT FALSE), `actor_id` (BIGINT, REFERENCES `users` ON DELETE SET NULL, optional), `object_id` (BIGINT, optional), `created_at` (TIMESTAMPTZ, NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW()).\n  - **Database Indexes**:\n    - `idx_notifications_user_id_created_at`: An index on `user_id` and `created_at` (descending) for efficient retrieval of notifications for a specific user, ordered by recency.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Database Migration: Defines schema changes for new features.\n  - ENUM Type: Uses a custom ENUM for structured notification types.\n  - Foreign Keys: Establishes relationships between `notifications` and `users` tables.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/config/config.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/config/config.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the application's configuration structure and provides a function to load these settings from environment variables, with support for `.env` files.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `Config`: Holds all application configuration parameters.\n      - Fields: `Port` (int), `DatabaseURL` (string), `RedisAddress` (string), `JWTSecretKey` (string), `AccessTokenExpiry` (time.Duration), `RefreshTokenExpiry` (time.Duration), `MaxGroupMembers` (int).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `Load() (*Config, error)`: Public function to load configuration from environment variables. It attempts to load from a `.env` file, then reads specific environment variables, provides default values, and performs necessary type conversions (e.g., string to int, string to time.Duration). It returns an error if critical variables like `DATABASE_URL` or `JWT_SECRET_KEY` are not set or if parsing fails.\n    - `getEnv(key, fallback string) string`: Internal helper function to retrieve an environment variable by `key` or return a `fallback` value if not found.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Configuration Management: Centralized loading and parsing of application settings.\n  - Environment Variable-based Configuration: Prioritizes environment variables, falls back to defaults.\n  - `godotenv` Integration: Supports `.env` files for local development.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/logger/logger.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/logger/logger.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a utility function to create a structured logger using Go's `slog` package.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `New(w io.Writer) *slog.Logger`: Public function that creates and returns a new `slog.Logger` instance. It configures the logger to use a JSON handler and sets the default logging level to `LevelDebug`.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/auth.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/auth.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides an HTTP middleware function to authenticate requests using JWT tokens, extracting the user ID and adding it to the request context.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `Auth(jwtSecret string) func(http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. It extracts a JWT token from either the `Authorization` header (Bearer token) or a `auth` query parameter (for WebSockets), validates it, and if valid, adds the `UserID` from the claims to the request context.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Middleware: Implements the standard `http.Handler` interface for chaining request processing.\n  - JWT Authentication: Uses `util.ValidateToken` to verify the token's signature and claims.\n  - Token Extraction: Supports extracting tokens from both `Authorization` headers and URL query parameters.\n  - Context Enrichment: Adds the authenticated `user_id` to the request context for downstream handlers.\n  - Error Handling: Returns `401 Unauthorized` for missing or invalid tokens.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/logger.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/logger.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides an HTTP middleware that logs details of incoming requests and their responses using Go's structured logging (`slog`) package.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewStructuredLogger(logger *slog.Logger) func(next http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. This middleware wraps the `http.ResponseWriter` to capture the HTTP status code and bytes written. It logs request details (method, path, status, duration, response size, request ID) at the `Info` level after the request has been served.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Middleware: Implements the standard `http.Handler` interface for chaining request processing.\n  - Structured Logging: Uses `slog` for consistent, machine-readable log output, which is beneficial for monitoring and analysis.\n  - Request Context: Retrieves the request ID (`req_id`) from the request context, typically set by another middleware (e.g., `chi_middleware.RequestID`).\n  - Response Wrapping: Uses `chi_middleware.NewWrapResponseWriter` to intercept and record response details before they are sent to the client.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/ratelimit.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/middleware/ratelimit.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides an HTTP middleware for rate limiting incoming requests based on the client's IP address, using a token bucket algorithm.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `IPRateLimiter`: Manages a collection of `rate.Limiter` instances, one for each unique IP address.\n      - Fields: `ips` (map[string]*rate.Limiter, stores limiters), `mu` (*sync.RWMutex, protects the map), `r` (rate.Limit, rate of tokens per second), `b` (int, burst size).\n  - **Variables**:\n    - `limiter`: A package-level `IPRateLimiter` instance, initialized with a default rate of 1 request/second and a burst of 3.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewIPRateLimiter(r rate.Limit, b int) *IPRateLimiter`: Public constructor for `IPRateLimiter`.\n    - `AddIP(ip string) *rate.Limiter`: Public method to create and add a new rate limiter for a given IP address.\n    - `GetLimiter(ip string) *rate.Limiter`: Public method to retrieve an existing rate limiter for an IP, or create a new one if it doesn't exist.\n    - `RateLimiter(requestsPerSecond float64, burst int) func(http.Handler) http.Handler`: Public function that returns an `http.Handler` middleware. This middleware extracts the client's IP address, checks if the request is allowed by the corresponding rate limiter, and if not, returns an `http.StatusTooManyRequests` (429) error.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - HTTP Middleware: Implements the standard `http.Handler` interface for chaining request processing.\n  - Rate Limiting: Uses `golang.org/x/time/rate` for a token bucket algorithm to control request frequency.\n  - Concurrency Safety: Employs `sync.RWMutex` to safely manage concurrent access to the map of IP-specific rate limiters.\n  - IP-based Limiting: Applies rate limits individually per client IP address.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/util/hash.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/util/hash.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for securely hashing passwords and comparing plain text passwords against hashes using bcrypt.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `HashPassword(password string) (string, error)`: Public function that takes a plain text password and returns its bcrypt hash.\n    - `CheckPasswordHash(password, hash string) bool`: Public function that compares a plain text password with a bcrypt hash, returning `true` if they match, `false` otherwise.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/pkg/util/token.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/pkg/util/token.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides utility functions for generating and validating JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) with custom claims.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `JWTClaims`: Custom claims structure for JWTs, embedding `jwt.RegisteredClaims`.\n      - Fields: `UserID` (int64), `jwt.RegisteredClaims`.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `GenerateToken(userID int64, expiry time.Duration, secretKey string) (string, error)`: Public function that creates a new JWT for a given user ID, expiry duration, and secret key.\n    - `ValidateToken(tokenString string, secretKey string) (*JWTClaims, error)`: Public function that parses and validates a JWT string using the provided secret key. Returns the `JWTClaims` if valid, or an error otherwise.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/.gitignore": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/.gitignore`\n- High-Level Purpose: Specifies files and directories that Git should ignore in the `quikchat-frontend` project.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a configuration file and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Standard Ignore Patterns: Includes common entries like `node_modules/`, `dist/`, and `.env`.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/package.json": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/package.json`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the project metadata, scripts, and development dependencies for the QuikChat frontend application, primarily for building and watching Tailwind CSS.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Variables / Constants**:\n    - `name`: \"quikchat-frontend\"\n    - `version`: \"1.0.0\"\n    - `description`: \"Frontend for QuikChat\"\n    - `main`: \"src/index.js\"\n    - `license`: \"ISC\"\n  - **Scripts**:\n    - `build:css`: Runs `tailwindcss` to compile `input.css` into `public/tailwind.css`.\n    - `watch:css`: Runs `tailwindcss` in watch mode for continuous compilation during development.\n    - `build`: Alias for `build:css`.\n    - `dev`: Alias for `watch:css`.\n  - **Dependencies**:\n    - `devDependencies`:\n      - `autoprefixer`: PostCSS plugin to add vendor prefixes.\n      - `postcss`: Tool for transforming CSS with JavaScript plugins.\n      - `tailwindcss`: A utility-first CSS framework.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Node.js Project Configuration: Standard `package.json` for managing a JavaScript project.\n  - Tailwind CSS Integration: Scripts are set up to build and watch Tailwind CSS for styling.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/postcss.config.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/postcss.config.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Configures PostCSS to process CSS files, specifically integrating Tailwind CSS and Autoprefixer.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a configuration file and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - PostCSS Plugin Configuration: Specifies `tailwindcss` and `autoprefixer` as PostCSS plugins.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/public/index.html": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/public/index.html`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main HTML file for the QuikChat frontend application, serving as the entry point for the browser. It sets up the basic page structure, links the compiled Tailwind CSS stylesheet, and loads the main JavaScript application bundle.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **HTML Structure**:\n    - `\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e`: Standard HTML5 doctype.\n    - `\u003chtml lang=\"en\" class=\"h-full bg-gray-900\"\u003e`: Sets language and initial Tailwind CSS classes for full height and dark background.\n    - `\u003chead\u003e`: Contains metadata, title, and stylesheet link.\n      - `\u003cmeta charset=\"UTF-8\"\u003e`, `\u003cmeta name=\"viewport\"\u003e`: Standard meta tags.\n      - `\u003ctitle\u003eQuikChat\u003c/title\u003e`: Page title.\n      - `\u003clink href=\"/tailwind.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\"\u003e`: Links the compiled Tailwind CSS stylesheet.\n    - `\u003cbody class=\"h-full\"\u003e`: Sets body to full height.\n      - `\u003cdiv id=\"app\" class=\"h-full\"\u003e`: The main container where JavaScript components will be dynamically rendered by the SPA framework.\n      - `\u003cscript type=\"module\" src=\"/src/index.js\"\u003e\u003c/script\u003e`: Imports the main JavaScript application as an ES module.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Entry Point: A minimal HTML file that relies heavily on JavaScript for rendering content and managing UI.\n  - Tailwind CSS Integration: Links the generated CSS file for styling.\n  - Module Script: Uses `type=\"module\"` for modern JavaScript module loading, enabling features like `import`/`export`.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/auth.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/auth.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides functions to interact with the backend's authentication API endpoints for user registration and login.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `handleResponse(response)`: Internal helper function that checks if an HTTP response is OK, parses the JSON, and throws an error if the response status is not successful.\n    - `register(username, password)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a POST request to the `/auth/register` endpoint with user credentials.\n    - `login(username, password)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a POST request to the `/auth/login` endpoint with user credentials.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/friends.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/friends.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides asynchronous functions to interact with the backend API for managing friend relationships and requests.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `listFriends()`: Public asynchronous function that fetches the current user's list of friends.\n    - `listIncomingRequests()`: Public asynchronous function that fetches pending friend requests sent to the current user.\n    - `sendFriendRequest(username)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a friend request to a specified username.\n    - `respondToRequest(requestID, action)`: Public asynchronous function that responds to a friend request (accept or decline) by its ID.\n    - `unfriend(username)`: Public asynchronous function that removes a friend by their username.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - API Client: Encapsulates `fetch` calls to specific friend-related endpoints.\n  - Authentication: Uses `getAccessToken()` to include a Bearer token in request headers for authorization.\n  - Error Handling: Leverages `handleResponse` (imported from `auth.js`) for consistent API response processing.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/groups.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/groups.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides asynchronous functions to interact with the backend API for group management, specifically for creating and searching groups.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `handleResponse(response)`: Internal asynchronous helper function that checks if an HTTP response is successful (`response.ok`). If not, it attempts to parse an error message from the JSON response and throws an `Error`. Otherwise, it parses and returns the JSON body.\n    - `createGroup(name, tag, description)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a POST request to the `/groups` endpoint to create a new group. It includes `name`, `tag`, and `description` in the request body and requires an authorization token.\n    - `searchGroups(tag)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a GET request to the `/groups/search` endpoint, including a `tag` query parameter to search for groups. It requires an authorization token.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - API Client: Encapsulates `fetch` calls to specific group-related endpoints.\n  - Authentication: Uses `getAccessToken()` (imported from `authStore.js`) to include a Bearer token in request headers for authorization.\n  - Error Handling: Centralizes API response error handling through the `handleResponse` utility.",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/messages.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/messages.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides asynchronous functions to interact with the backend API for sending, fetching messages, and managing media uploads.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `fetchMessages(conversationId, cursor = null)`: Public asynchronous function that fetches a list of messages for a given conversation, supporting cursor-based pagination.\n    - `sendMessage(conversationId, message)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a new message (text or media) to a specified conversation.\n    - `getPresignedUrl(filename)`: Public asynchronous function that requests a presigned URL from the backend for uploading a file.\n    - `uploadFile(uploadUrl, file)`: Public asynchronous function that uploads a file directly to a given presigned URL (e.g., S3).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - API Client: Encapsulates `fetch` calls to specific message-related endpoints.\n  - Authentication: Uses `getAccessToken()` to include a Bearer token in request headers for authorization.\n  - Error Handling: Leverages `handleResponse` (imported from `auth.js`) for consistent API response processing.\n  - Media Upload: Separates getting a presigned URL from the actual file upload.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/notifications.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/notifications.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides asynchronous functions to interact with the backend API for fetching, marking, and counting user notifications.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `handleResponse(response)`: Internal asynchronous helper function that checks if an HTTP response is successful (`response.ok`). If not, it attempts to parse an error message from the JSON response and throws an `Error`. Otherwise, it parses and returns the JSON body, or `null` for 204 No Content responses.\n    - `getNotifications(limit = 20, offset = 0)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a GET request to `/notifications` to fetch a paginated list of notifications for the current user.\n    - `markAsRead(notificationId)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a POST request to `/notifications/{notificationId}/read` to mark a specific notification as read.\n    - `markAllAsRead()`: Public asynchronous function that sends a POST request to `/notifications/read-all` to mark all unread notifications for the current user as read.\n    - `getUnreadCount()`: Public asynchronous function that sends a GET request to `/notifications/unread-count` to fetch the total count of unread notifications for the current user.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - API Client: Encapsulates `fetch` calls to specific notification-related endpoints.\n  - Authentication: Uses `getAccessToken()` (imported from `authStore.js`) to include a Bearer token in request headers for authorization.\n  - Error Handling: Centralizes API response error handling through the `handleResponse` utility.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/api/users.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/api/users.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides asynchronous functions to interact with the backend API for user profile management and blocking.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `API_BASE_URL`: Module-level constant defining the base URL for API requests.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `getProfile(username)`: Public asynchronous function that fetches a user's profile by username.\n    - `updateProfile(profileData)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a PUT request to update the current user's profile.\n    - `blockUser(username)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a POST request to block a specified user.\n    - `unblockUser(username)`: Public asynchronous function that sends a DELETE request to unblock a specified user.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - API Client: Encapsulates `fetch` calls to specific user-related endpoints.\n  - Authentication: Uses `getAccessToken()` to include a Bearer token in request headers for authorization.\n  - Error Handling: Leverages `handleResponse` (imported from `auth.js`) for consistent API response processing.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/components/MessageDisplay.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/components/MessageDisplay.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders a single chat message component, displaying its content, sender, and timestamp, with different styling for own messages.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `MessageDisplay({ message, isOwnMessage })`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing a single message. It dynamically applies CSS classes based on whether the message was sent by the current user.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and styles a DOM element.\n  - Conditional Rendering/Styling: Adjusts layout and colors based on the `isOwnMessage` prop.\n  - Data Display: Formats and displays message content, sender name, and timestamp.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/components/Navbar.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/components/Navbar.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders the navigation bar for the QuikChat frontend, providing links to different application pages (Chat, Friends, Notifications, Profile) and a logout button. It also displays a dynamic badge showing the count of unread notifications.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `Navbar()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the navigation bar.\n      - It dynamically creates and styles `nav`, `h1` (application title), and `div` (container for navigation links) elements.\n      - Creates `a` elements for navigation links: `Chat`, `Friends`, `Notifications`, `Profile`.\n      - Creates a `button` for `Logout` which dispatches a custom `logout` event when clicked.\n      - Includes a `notificationBadge` span element, which is dynamically updated to show the unread notification count and is hidden if the count is zero.\n      - `updateBadge(count)`: Internal function to update the `notificationBadge`'s text content and visibility based on the provided `count`.\n      - **Lifecycle \u0026 Integration**:\n        - Fetches the initial unread notification count using `getUnreadCount()` from `notifications.js`.\n        - Subscribes to `notificationStore` updates to reactively update the `notificationBadge` whenever the unread count changes.\n        - Uses a `MutationObserver` to detect when the `Navbar` component is removed from the DOM, ensuring the `notificationStore` subscription is cleaned up.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and manages DOM elements.\n  - UI State Management: Integrates with `notificationStore` to display and react to changes in the unread notification count.\n  - API Interaction: Calls `getUnreadCount` from `notifications.js`.\n  - Event Handling: Dispatches a custom `logout` event for application-wide logout handling.\n  - Conditional Rendering/Styling: Dynamically shows/hides and updates the notification badge.\n  - Component Cleanup: Uses `MutationObserver` to manage subscriptions when the component is unmounted.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/components/NotificationItem.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/components/NotificationItem.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders a single notification item component for display in the frontend.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NotificationItem({ notification })`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing a single notification. It dynamically applies CSS classes based on the notification's `read` status, displays the message, actor's profile image (or a placeholder), and the creation timestamp. It also shows a blue dot for unread notifications.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and styles a DOM element.\n  - Conditional Rendering/Styling: Adjusts appearance (opacity, unread indicator) based on the `notification.read` property.\n  - Data Display: Formats and displays notification content and metadata.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/index.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/index.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: The main entry point for the QuikChat frontend application, responsible for client-side routing, authentication checks, and initializing global services like WebSocket.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `routes`: Object mapping URL hash paths (e.g., '/', '/login') to their corresponding page components.\n    - `protectedRoutes`: Array of hash paths that require a user to be authenticated.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `router()`: Public function that serves as the client-side router. It listens for `hashchange` and `DOMContentLoaded` events, determines the current path, clears the app container, enforces authentication for protected routes, renders the `Navbar` (if authenticated), connects/disconnects the `WebSocketService`, and renders the appropriate page component.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Routing: Implements client-side routing using `window.location.hash`.\n  - Authentication Guard: Checks `isAuthenticated()` before rendering protected routes, redirecting to `/login` if unauthorized.\n  - Global Event Handling: Attaches listeners for browser events and a custom `logout` event.\n  - Component Rendering: Dynamically renders page components into the `#app` DOM element.\n  - WebSocket Integration: Connects/disconnects `WebSocketService` based on authentication status.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/pages/ChatPage.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/pages/ChatPage.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders the main chat interface, including a placeholder conversation list, a scrollable message display area, and an input form for sending text and media messages. It integrates with backend APIs and WebSocket for real-time updates and supports message pagination.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `CURRENT_USER_ID`: (number) Hardcoded user ID retrieved from local storage for demonstration.\n    - `CONVERSATION_ID`: (number) Hardcoded conversation ID for demonstration purposes.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `ChatPage()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the chat page.\n      - **Internal State Variables**: `isLoading` (boolean), `hasMoreMessages` (boolean), `lastMessageId` (number|null) to manage message loading and pagination.\n      - `renderMessages(messages, prepend = false)`: Internal function to dynamically create and append/prepend `MessageDisplay` components to the messages list.\n      - `loadMoreMessages()`: Internal asynchronous function that fetches older messages from the API using cursor-based pagination when the user scrolls to the \"top\" (visually bottom due to `flex-col-reverse`) of the messages container.\n      - **Event Handlers**:\n        - Scroll event listener on `messagesContainer`: Triggers `loadMoreMessages`.\n        - Form submit event listener: Handles sending text messages via `sendMessage` API.\n        - File input change event listener: Handles media file selection, orchestrates getting a presigned URL from the backend, uploading the file to S3, and then sending a media message.\n      - **Lifecycle \u0026 Integration**:\n        - Subscribes to `chatStore` for real-time message updates, re-rendering the message list when the store changes.\n        - Performs an initial fetch of messages and adds them to `chatStore`.\n        - Calls `connectWebSocket()` to establish a real-time connection for live updates.\n        - Uses a `MutationObserver` to detect when the `ChatPage` component is removed from the DOM, ensuring proper cleanup (unsubscribing from `chatStore` and disconnecting the observer).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and manages DOM elements.\n  - UI State Management: Integrates with `chatStore` for managing and reacting to message data changes.\n  - API Interaction: Utilizes `fetchMessages`, `sendMessage`, `getPresignedUrl`, `uploadFile` from `messages.js`.\n  - WebSocket Integration: Connects to `WebSocketService` for real-time message delivery.\n  - Infinite Scrolling/Pagination: Implements logic to load older messages on demand.\n  - Media Upload Workflow: Handles the multi-step process of secure file uploads.\n  - Component Cleanup: Uses `MutationObserver` to manage subscriptions and observers when the component is unmounted.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/pages/FriendsPage.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/pages/FriendsPage.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders the user interface for managing friends and friend requests, displaying incoming requests and the current friends list.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `FriendsPage()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the friends and requests page. It fetches and displays incoming friend requests and the user's friends list, providing buttons to accept or decline requests.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and manipulates DOM elements to build the page.\n  - UI State Management: Displays \"Loading...\" and then populates lists based on API responses.\n  - API Interaction: Calls `listFriends`, `listIncomingRequests`, and `respondToRequest` from `friends.js`.\n  - Event Handling: Attaches `onclick` handlers to accept/decline buttons to interact with the API and update the UI.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders the login and registration forms, handles user input, interacts with the authentication API, and manages local authentication state.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `LoginPage()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the login/registration page. It sets up event listeners for form submission (login and register) and a toggle link to switch between the two forms. It calls `login` or `register` API functions and `setTokens` on success.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Returns a dynamically created DOM element.\n  - Form Handling: Manages form input and submission for both login and registration.\n  - UI State Management: Toggles visibility and text content based on `isLogin` state.\n  - API Interaction: Calls `login` and `register` functions from `auth.js`.\n  - Client-side Routing: Redirects to '/' on successful authentication.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/pages/NotificationPage.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/pages/NotificationPage.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders the user interface for displaying and managing notifications, allowing users to view and mark notifications as read.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NotificationPage()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the notifications page. It initializes the UI, fetches notifications using `getNotifications`, renders them using `NotificationItem` components, and attaches event listeners to mark individual notifications as read. It also subscribes to `notificationStore` for real-time updates and cleans up the subscription on page removal.\n    - `loadNotifications()`: Internal asynchronous function to fetch notifications from the API and update the `notificationStore`.\n    - `renderNotifications(notifications)`: Internal function to clear the notification list and render the provided array of notifications into the UI.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and manipulates DOM elements to build the page.\n  - UI State Management: Integrates with `notificationStore` to display and react to notification data changes.\n  - API Interaction: Calls `getNotifications` and `markAsRead` from `notifications.js`.\n  - Event Handling: Attaches `click` listeners to notification items to mark them as read.\n  - Lifecycle Management: Cleans up the store subscription when the component is removed from the DOM.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/pages/ProfilePage.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/pages/ProfilePage.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Renders a user's profile page, displaying their username, display name, join date, and placeholder action buttons.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `ProfilePage()`: Public function that returns a DOM element representing the user profile page. It fetches profile data (currently hardcoded to 'me' or 'testuser' for simplicity) and displays it, along with placeholder buttons for actions like \"Edit Profile\", \"Add Friend\", and \"Block User\".\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Single Page Application (SPA) Component: Dynamically creates and styles DOM elements.\n  - API Interaction: Calls `getProfile` from `users.js` to fetch user data.\n  - Placeholder Functionality: Buttons are present but do not yet have full functionality implemented.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/services/WebSocketService.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/services/WebSocketService.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages the WebSocket connection to the backend for real-time updates, handling connection lifecycle, message parsing, and dispatching updates to relevant stores.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Variables**:\n    - `socket`: Module-level variable storing the active WebSocket instance.\n    - `reconnectInterval`: Module-level constant (number) defining the delay before attempting to reconnect.\n    - `shouldReconnect`: Module-level flag (boolean) indicating whether the service should attempt to reconnect on close.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `connect()`: Public function to establish a WebSocket connection. It retrieves the access token, constructs the WebSocket URL, and sets up event handlers for `onopen`, `onmessage`, `onclose`, and `onerror`. It also implements an automatic reconnection mechanism.\n    - `disconnect()`: Public function to explicitly close the WebSocket connection and prevent further reconnection attempts.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - WebSocket Client: Manages the lifecycle of a WebSocket connection.\n  - Reconnection Logic: Automatically attempts to reconnect after a delay if the connection closes unexpectedly.\n  - Real-time State Updates: Parses incoming JSON messages and dispatches them to `chatStore` for new messages and `notificationStore` for new notifications.\n  - Authentication: Includes the access token as a query parameter for WebSocket authentication.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/store/authStore.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/store/authStore.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Manages the storage and retrieval of authentication tokens (access and refresh tokens) using browser's `localStorage`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `ACCESS_TOKEN_KEY`: String constant for the access token key in local storage.\n    - `REFRESH_TOKEN_KEY`: String constant for the refresh token key in local storage.\n  - **Variables**:\n    - `accessToken`: Module-level variable storing the current access token, initialized from local storage.\n    - `refreshToken`: Module-level variable storing the current refresh token, initialized from local storage.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `setTokens(newAccessToken, newRefreshToken)`: Public function that updates the `accessToken` and `refreshToken` variables and persists them to `localStorage`.\n    - `getAccessToken()`: Public function that returns the current `accessToken`.\n    - `getRefreshToken()`: Public function that returns the current `refreshToken`.\n    - `logout()`: Public function that clears the `accessToken` and `refreshToken` variables and removes them from `localStorage`.\n    - `isAuthenticated()`: Public function that returns `true` if an `accessToken` is present, indicating a user is logged in.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Client-side State Management: Uses module-level variables and `localStorage` for simple authentication state.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/store/chatStore.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/store/chatStore.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a simple, in-memory state management solution for chat conversations and messages in the frontend.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Variables**:\n    - `state`: Module-level object holding the current chat state (conversations, messages, active conversation ID).\n    - `listeners`: Array to store functions subscribed to state changes.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `subscribe(listener)`: Public function to add a listener that will be called when the state changes. Returns an `unsubscribe` function.\n    - `notify()`: Internal function to call all registered listeners.\n    - `addMessage(conversationId, message)`: Public function to add a new message to a specific conversation, preventing duplicates.\n    - `prependMessages(conversationId, messages)`: Public function to add messages to the beginning of a conversation's message list (e.g., for loading older messages).\n    - `setActiveConversation(conversationId)`: Public function to set the currently active conversation.\n    - `getState()`: Public function to retrieve the current state object.\n  - **Exports**:\n    - `chatStore`: An object exposing the public state management functions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Simple State Management: Uses a basic publish-subscribe pattern.\n  - In-memory Store: Stores application state directly in JavaScript memory.\n  - Immutability (partial): Updates state by creating new arrays for messages to trigger reactivity.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/store/notificationStore.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/store/notificationStore.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a simple, in-memory state management solution for notifications in the frontend, including a list of notifications and an unread count.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Variables**:\n    - `state`: Module-level object holding the current notification state, including `notifications` (array) and `unreadCount` (number).\n    - `listeners`: A `Set` to store functions subscribed to state changes.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `subscribe(listener)`: Public function to add a listener that will be called when the state changes. Returns an `unsubscribe` function.\n    - `notify()`: Internal function to call all registered listeners with the current state.\n    - `setNotifications(notifications)`: Public function to replace the entire list of notifications in the state.\n    - `addNotification(notification)`: Public function to add a new notification to the beginning of the list and increment the `unreadCount`.\n    - `setUnreadCount(count)`: Public function to explicitly set the `unreadCount`.\n    - `decrementUnreadCount()`: Public function to decrement the `unreadCount`, ensuring it does not go below zero.\n    - `markNotificationAsReadInState(notificationId)`: Public function to find a notification by ID, mark it as read in the state, and decrement the `unreadCount` if it was previously unread.\n    - `getState()`: Public function to retrieve the current state object.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Simple State Management: Uses a basic publish-subscribe pattern for state changes.\n  - In-memory Store: Stores application state directly in JavaScript memory.\n  - Immutability (partial): Updates state by creating new arrays for notifications to trigger reactivity.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/styles/input.css": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/styles/input.css`\n- High-Level Purpose: Serves as the main entry point for Tailwind CSS, importing its base, component, and utility styles.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a CSS file and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Tailwind CSS Directives: Uses `@tailwind` directives to inject Tailwind's pre-generated styles.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/types/types.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/types/types.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines JSDoc type definitions for common data structures used in the QuikChat frontend, such as `User` and `Message`.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Types**:\n    - `User`: JSDoc typedef for a user object.\n      - Properties: `id` (number), `username` (string), `display_name` (string), `profile_image_url` (string|null), `created_at` (string), `updated_at` (string), `last_seen_at` (string|null).\n    - `Message`: JSDoc typedef for a message object.\n      - Properties: `id` (number), `conversation_id` (number), `sender_id` (number), `type` ('text' | 'media'), `content` (string), `created_at` (string), `sender` (User, optional).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - JSDoc Type Definitions: Provides type hints for JavaScript code, improving readability and tooling support without requiring TypeScript compilation.\n",
  "quikchat-frontend/src/utils/dom.js": "- File Path: `quikchat-frontend/src/utils/dom.js`\n- High-Level Purpose: Provides a utility function to render a given component into the main application root element.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `appElement`: Module-level constant referencing the DOM element with `id=\"app\"`.\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `render(component)`: Public function that clears the content of the `#app` element and appends the result of calling the provided `component` function.\n",
